Accept MethodParameters entries that have no name.

A name_index of zero is legal and means the parameter has no name (JVMS
4.7.24). javac 21 and later write such entries for mandated and synthetic
parameters: an enum's valueOf and constructor, an inner class
constructor's outer instance. jd-core read every name from the constant
pool, so any class with one of those failed with a NullPointerException
in ConstantPool.getConstantUtf8.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/jd/core/v1/service/deserializer/classfile/ClassFileDeserializer.java b/src/main/java/org/jd/core/v1/service/deserializer/classfile/ClassFileDeserializer.java
index 09b99a2..b5e5005 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/jd/core/v1/service/deserializer/classfile/ClassFileDeserializer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/jd/core/v1/service/deserializer/classfile/ClassFileDeserializer.java
@@ -565,7 +565,7 @@ public class ClassFileDeserializer {
         for (int i=0; i<count; i++) {
             int nameIndex = reader.readUnsignedShort();
 
-            String name = constants.getConstantUtf8(nameIndex);
+            String name = (nameIndex == 0) ? null : constants.getConstantUtf8(nameIndex);
 
             parameters[i] = new MethodParameter(name, reader.readUnsignedShort());
         }
